# VCR Cassette Ownership

RULE: The six interfaces (unified-market-interface, unified-trade-execution-interface, unified-sports-execution-interface, unified-reference-data-interface, unified-position-interface, unified-cloud-interface) perform VCR recording and live schema validation in their integration tests; they hold API keys. unified-api-contracts (AC) holds schemas and static examples only. Consumers reference cassettes by path — never duplicate.
WHY: Single source of truth for schemas in AC; interfaces own live verification and keys; prevents cassette drift.
CODEX: 02-data/vcr-cassette-ownership.md

DO:
 # In an interface repo: record/validate with live API keys (interface holds keys)
 # Use cassette_library_dir or path to AC mocks (unified_api_contracts_external/<venue>/mocks/)
 import vcr
 cassette_dir = Path("../unified-api-contracts/unified_api_contracts/unified_api_contracts_external")  # or interface-owned mocks
 @vcr.use_cassette(str(cassette_dir / "binance/mocks/ticker_24hr.yaml"))
 def test_binance_ticker(): ...

## UCI VCR Tests (GCS + AWS both required)

unified-cloud-interface is the ONE repo allowed cloud-provider-specific code. It MUST have VCR integration tests for BOTH providers:

- `tests/integration/test_gcs_integration.py` — VCR cassettes for GCS Storage API calls
- `tests/integration/test_s3_integration.py` — VCR cassettes for AWS S3 API calls
- `tests/integration/test_gcp_secret_manager.py` — VCR cassettes for GCP Secret Manager
- `tests/integration/test_aws_secrets_manager.py` — VCR cassettes for AWS Secrets Manager

Cassettes validate that the UCI abstraction layer correctly routes to both providers.
Provider selection is controlled by `CLOUD_PROVIDER` env var (`gcp` or `aws`).

These tests prove the cloud-agnostic API works on both backends.

NEVER:
 Copy cassettes to consumer repos
 Use VCR for WebSocket (different tooling required)
 Use standard HTTP VCR for IBKR/TWS — TWS uses a proprietary socket protocol; mock at ib_insync object level instead (see ibkr-gateway-single-source.mdc)
 Run collect_responses / validate_schemas / live verification from AC (interfaces do that)
